# AppStoreFeed: the bridge between the store service and the App Store window. Never install/remove/update.
ipc panels appStore
wait 3
shot open
note Window opened and Discover is loaded or loading with sections and the search field has the caret (check in each look); no empty or broken window. Same as QML.
ipc panels close
wait 1
shot closed
note Window closed completely, nothing left on screen.
ipc panels appStore
wait 3
shot reopen
note Window reopens and Discover loads again exactly as the first time (state feed re-sent on reopen).
# Search each place (typed in the search field, which has the caret on open)
key firefox
wait 2
shot search
note Results answer for "firefox"; cards show logos and source names such as Arch repos, Flathub, AUR. Compare with QML (sandbox may have no network or catalogue so a notice may show instead; it must be the same in both shells).
key -M ctrl -k a -m ctrl -k BackSpace
key aur: yay
wait 2
shot search-aur
note AUR chip on, subtitle says Community packages from the AUR; cards show source "AUR - community" when an answer arrives. Same as QML.
# MANUAL: open Spotlight, type "gimp", choose its Get row with the store closed; store must open on that app's page; repeat with store open for another app and the page must switch
# MANUAL: on an app's page (Material) split menu > Copy the name, then wl-paste must give the name; Open the website must request a browser launch in the log
# MANUAL: without the catalogue the notice shows in both shells (needs an arena without a catalogue)
ipc panels close
